Lota's Core Audio patch, for iOS alone: one change to the read callback
of LÖVE's src/modules/sound/lullaby/CoreAudioDecoder.cpp, which LÖVE's
iOS build compiles with LOVE_SUPPORT_COREAUDIO so that a game loads AIFF
and AAC in M4A. The decoder opens its Stream with
AudioFileOpenWithCallbacks (line 66), which asks its read callback for
requestCount bytes at the offset inPosition, and Audio File Services
reads a file's header, chunks, and packets at offsets of its own
choosing. readFunc (lines 38-45) ignores inPosition and reads from
wherever the Stream is, so after the first read every one returns bytes
from the wrong place: on an iPhone 12 mini and in the iOS Simulator, an
M4A failed with "No suitable audio decoders found", and an AIFF of 1.5 s
at 48000 Hz came out as 0.07 s at 22050 Hz from a decoder that mistook
it (doc/contributors/upstream/026.md). The callback honoured the offset
until LÖVE's commit c09fef8e79c887aab96628f452bb142eebcddcf7 ("Audio
source decoding improvements") moved decoders from a Data, which it
copied from at data->getData() + inPosition, to a Stream.

This patch seeks the Stream to inPosition before each read, and reports
a seek that fails as the position error Audio File Services expects, with
nothing read; it changes nothing else. With it, the same iPhone decoded
both files at 48000 Hz, 1.5 s long, as afinfo describes them.

Nothing in Lota can do this: readFunc is static in CoreAudioDecoder.cpp,
and Sound::newDecoder hands the decoder LÖVE's own Stream, so no code of
Lota's chooses where the callback reads. CMake applies the patch only
when it builds the engine for iOS, the only target that compiles the
decoder, as LÖVE's liblove-ios target alone does, to a copy of the file
in the build tree (ext/lota/engine/CMakeLists.txt); vendor/love is never
written to.

diff -ruN a/src/modules/sound/lullaby/CoreAudioDecoder.cpp b/src/modules/sound/lullaby/CoreAudioDecoder.cpp
--- a/src/modules/sound/lullaby/CoreAudioDecoder.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/sound/lullaby/CoreAudioDecoder.cpp
@@ -38,6 +38,13 @@
 static OSStatus readFunc(void *inClientData, SInt64 inPosition, UInt32 requestCount, void *buffer, UInt32 *actualCount)
 {
 	auto stream = (Stream *) inClientData;
+	// Read where Audio File Services asks (ext/lota/engine/coreaudio.patch).
+	if (!stream->seek(inPosition))
+	{
+		*actualCount = 0;
+		return kAudioFilePositionError;
+	}
+
 	int64 readbytes = stream->read(buffer, requestCount);
 
 	*actualCount = (UInt32) readbytes;
